WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:01.666
It is three in the morning.

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:04.046
Start-up is planned for six.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:07.274
Maintenance records show a transmitter being calibrated.

00:00:07.665 --> 00:00:09.120
An alarm is inhibited.

00:00:09.511 --> 00:00:11.651
A temporary bypass remains open.

00:00:12.134 --> 00:00:14.414
Each record tells part of the story.

00:00:14.805 --> 00:00:17.818
The question for the person taking the shift is more important:

00:00:18.229 --> 00:00:21.727
what protection is actually available, and what has changed since the

00:00:21.747 --> 00:00:22.697
hazard study?

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.720
Veriso Barrier connects the hazard study to the operating life of

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:30.636
the plant. It brings the study, protective functions,

00:00:30.745 --> 00:00:35.266
equipment, checks and changes into one operator record.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.111
Engineers can trace the intended protection.

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:41.048
Operations can see its current declared condition.

00:00:41.532 --> 00:00:45.029
Owners can see what needs attention, who is responsible and when

00:00:45.049 --> 00:00:46.882
a temporary arrangement expires.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.307
The work can begin before a HAZOP.

00:00:49.628 --> 00:00:54.395
Project information, process descriptions and relevant reference templates

00:00:54.678 --> 00:00:59.399
help prepare a structured first draft: proposed nodes, parameters,

00:00:59.624 --> 00:01:02.612
deviations and questions for the study team.

00:01:03.188 --> 00:01:06.385
Existing assumptions and missing information remain visible.

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:09.542
This gives the team an organised starting point for a hazard

00:01:09.562 --> 00:01:13.914
and operability study, with room for engineering judgement and challenge.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:18.773
The study team examines deviations from design intent, considers causes and

00:01:18.793 --> 00:01:22.999
consequences, challenges safeguards and records actions.

00:01:23.263 --> 00:01:27.271
For our vessel, a pressure deviation opens a discussion about how

00:01:27.291 --> 00:01:30.499
containment could be lost and what would prevent or limit the

00:01:30.519 --> 00:01:35.376
outcome. Decisions, assumptions and actions belong to the team.

00:01:35.952 --> 00:01:39.724
Veriso keeps their structure and origin visible as the study develops.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.712
Existing studies can enter through signed documents, spreadsheets or scanned

00:01:44.732 --> 00:01:49.193
records. The converter structures the content and retains the link to

00:01:49.213 --> 00:01:50.866
the original document and row.

00:01:51.257 --> 00:01:53.397
An engineer reviews the interpretation.

00:01:53.718 --> 00:01:57.507
Unreadable or uncertain material is surfaced for resolution.

00:01:57.991 --> 00:02:01.326
The result is a usable study record whose meaning can always

00:02:01.346 --> 00:02:03.097
be checked against its source.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.202
For major-accident scenarios, the study becomes a bow tie.

00:02:07.686 --> 00:02:11.601
Causes sit on the left, consequences on the right, and the

00:02:11.621 --> 00:02:13.715
loss of control sits between them.

00:02:14.292 --> 00:02:18.197
Prevention and mitigation barriers sit on the paths they protect.

00:02:18.681 --> 00:02:22.589
The linked register shows the protective function, supporting equipment,

00:02:22.872 --> 00:02:24.501
ownership and checks.

00:02:24.892 --> 00:02:28.489
Candidate safety-critical equipment is identified for engineering review.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:32.857
A barrier diagram is only useful if its dependencies are understood.

00:02:33.341 --> 00:02:37.547
Two apparent protections may depend on the same transmitter, the same

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:39.452
logic or the same person.

00:02:40.145 --> 00:02:42.366
Veriso connects these relationships.

00:02:42.687 --> 00:02:46.034
A change to one shared dependency can then be traced across

00:02:46.054 --> 00:02:47.846
every affected protective function.

00:02:48.329 --> 00:02:51.572
The same temporary stand-in can also be recognised when it is

00:02:51.592 --> 00:02:53.378
being counted more than once.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:58.213
Maintenance, permits, overrides, change records and

00:02:58.233 --> 00:03:02.335
field checks connect through agreed interfaces and reporting windows.

00:03:02.726 --> 00:03:05.902
A work order is linked to the protective function it affects,

00:03:06.127 --> 00:03:08.743
with the effect reviewed under the operator's rules.

00:03:09.006 --> 00:03:12.342
If a source stops reporting, the gap remains visible.

00:03:12.826 --> 00:03:15.889
Silence does not become evidence that the barrier is healthy.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:20.152
When protection is impaired, the record follows the operator's authorisation

00:03:20.172 --> 00:03:24.997
process. It identifies the affected function, responsible owner,

00:03:25.223 --> 00:03:27.490
compensating measure and expiry.

00:03:28.183 --> 00:03:31.461
Temporary arrangements remain visible until properly resolved.

00:03:31.852 --> 00:03:34.828
Overdue measures and reused stand-ins demand attention.

00:03:35.311 --> 00:03:38.534
Where the operator classifies a protection as never to be impaired,

00:03:38.759 --> 00:03:41.463
that restriction remains part of the decision.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:44.622
Management of change follows the same connected record.

00:03:44.943 --> 00:03:48.874
A proposed change moves through technical review, risk assessment,

00:03:48.983 --> 00:03:53.863
authorisation, implementation and pre-start-up review before close-out.

00:03:54.439 --> 00:03:57.392
Temporary changes carry an expiry from the start.

00:03:57.969 --> 00:04:00.375
The link back to the study makes it possible to see

00:04:00.395 --> 00:04:04.625
whether the plant, its procedures and its protective arrangements still

00:04:04.645 --> 00:04:06.280
match the agreed basis.

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:09.554
Field checks test the declared picture against what is found on

00:04:09.574 --> 00:04:14.000
the plant. Checks can be scheduled by calendar, operating hours or

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:17.959
starts. The person carrying out the check records the finding and

00:04:17.979 --> 00:04:22.839
its evidence. Effective, partially effective, ineffective

00:04:22.948 --> 00:04:26.017
and not-yet-checked conditions stay distinguishable.

00:04:27.012 --> 00:04:30.121
A missing check cannot quietly become a positive result.

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:33.615
At handover, the picture becomes three clear views.

00:04:33.936 --> 00:04:35.264
Which barriers are out?

00:04:35.469 --> 00:04:38.364
Which lines of protection are thinner than the study intended?

00:04:38.754 --> 00:04:42.484
Which compensating measures are carrying the temporary burden, and when do

00:04:42.504 --> 00:04:45.828
they expire? Counts have stated totals.

00:04:46.092 --> 00:04:48.325
Critical conditions stay visible.

00:04:48.715 --> 00:04:53.032
A serious loss of protection cannot disappear inside an overall percentage.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.701
The manager can now make a decision under the plant's procedures

00:04:56.926 --> 00:04:58.845
with the affected protection in view.

00:04:59.329 --> 00:05:03.082
The record preserves what was known, what was decided and who

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:07.718
accepted responsibility. Over time, recurring inhibits,

00:05:07.827 --> 00:05:11.477
repeated extensions and failed checks reveal patterns.

00:05:12.053 --> 00:05:16.705
Those lessons return to engineering, maintenance and the next hazard study,

00:05:17.046 --> 00:05:19.970
so the operating record becomes a source of improvement.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:24.395
Veriso Barrier brings study intent, changing plant conditions and

00:05:24.415 --> 00:05:27.577
accountable decisions into one continuous picture.

00:05:28.153 --> 00:05:29.423
Convert the study.

00:05:29.744 --> 00:05:30.978
Confirm the model.

00:05:31.299 --> 00:05:32.580
Connect the records.

00:05:32.844 --> 00:05:33.973
Check the plant.

00:05:34.295 --> 00:05:35.819
Run the operating cycle.

00:05:36.083 --> 00:05:37.944
The operator remains in control.

00:05:38.265 --> 00:05:41.508
The value is clarity: protection that can be traced from the

00:05:41.528 --> 00:05:44.986
original hazard to the decision that matters on the next shift.
